    section: "C", questionRef: "2018 HL Q11(c)",
    questionText: "Answer the following questions from your knowledge of the human nervous system. (c)(i) Outline the role of each of the following in the transmission of a nerve impulse: 1. Dendrites 2. Axon 3. Cell body. (c)(ii) Describe how a nerve impulse is transmitted across a synaptic cleft, from one neuron to the next. (c)(iii) Explain the importance of the myelin sheath in the transmission of a nerve impulse. (24) [OVER]",
