    questionText: "The diagram below summarises some of the changes that take place in a typical human female during the menstrual cycle. Answer the questions that follow, based on this diagram. (a)(i) What is the role of the menstrual cycle? (a)(ii) Name the event that occurs between days 1‐5 of the cycle. (a)(iii) The event you have named at (ii) is triggered by a large drop in a certain hormone. Name the hormone. (a)(iv) Where is the hormone oestrogen produced? (a)(v) Using the time axis from the graph above, sketch a graph in your answer book, to indicate the changes in oestrogen levels during the cycle. (a)(vi) Name the event that occurs at day 14 and name the hormone which causes this to happen. (a)(vii) Name the structure that the Graafian follicle develops into after day 14. (a)(viii) Does the graph indicate that the woman became pregnant during this menstrual cycle? Explain your answer.",
